* Orange OR120 Graphic Mk II preamp (early 1970s, redrawn by B. Hickmott 2004): the input jack into V1a (ECC83, 2k2 / 50u cathode),
* the Orange tone circuit (68n, 1n5 / 10n treble pot, 1M bass pot with 2n2 and 22n, two 100k), the 1M log gain pot with its 330p, V2a
* (the same stage again) and the "FAC" six-position switch: a ladder of 4n7, 4n7, 2n2, 1n and 330p whose tap is the output, a
* high-pass that rises with the position. The 100k into the power amp's input is here as the load of the output node.
*
* Assumptions where the drawing is silent or ambiguous (change them here, not in code):
*  - the two input jacks are drawn each behind its own 68k, wired as the 1972 schematic (the drawing's author doubts it): one input
*    through 68k, 1M to ground at the grid;
*  - the six FAC positions: the wiper takes the node after V2's 68n (position 1, no capacitor) or a tap of the series ladder
*    (positions 2 to 6: 4n7; 4n7 + 4n7; ... + 2n2; ... + 1n; ... + 330p, all in series);
*  - the tone circuit: the bass pot's top is 100k from the 68n, its bottom 22k to ground, 2n2 from its top to the wiper and 22n from its
*    bottom to the wiper; the wiper goes through 100k to the treble pot's wiper; the treble pot has 1n5 on its top (from the 68n) and 10n
*    on its bottom; the gain pot's top is the treble pot's top, with 330p across to its wiper (V2's grid);
*  - supply: node x is D+ (the last 33k / 16u stage), driven from the power amp at run time.

.nodes x gin in g1 p1 k1 t0 n1 bw bb tw o1 tb g2 p2 k2 f1 f2 f3 f4 f5 f6 o pkb1 pkb2 pkk1 pkk2 pkk4

* D+ (node x): driven from the power amp at run time; 250 V is the standalone default.
V VRAIL x 100 250
* The guitar behind a variable source resistance.
I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p

* Input: 68k to the grid, 1M to ground.
R R68 in g1 68k
R R1M g1 0 1M

* V1a: 220k plate load from D+, 2k2 cathode with 50u.
T V1A g1 p1 k1 12AX7
R R220A x p1 220k
R RK1 k1 0 2k2
C CK1 k1 0 50u

* Tone circuit. 68n into the 100k and the 1n5; bass pot (1M log) with 22k to ground; treble pot (1M log) with 10n on its bottom.
C C68A p1 t0 68n
R R100T t0 n1 100k
R VR_BT n1 bw 1
R VR_BB bw bb 1
R R22K bb 0 22k
C C2N2 n1 bw 2n2
C C22N bb bw 22n
R R100W bw tw 100k
C C1N5 t0 o1 1n5
R VR_TT o1 tw 1
R VR_TB tw tb 1
C C10N tb 0 10n

* Gain pot (1M log) with 330p across its top section; the wiper is V2's grid.
C C330P o1 g2 330p
R VR_GT o1 g2 1
R VR_GB g2 0 1

* V2a: the same stage as V1a.
T V2A g2 p2 k2 12AX7
R R220B x p2 220k
R RK2 k2 0 2k2
C CK2 k2 0 50u

* 68n and the FAC ladder: caps in series from the 68n's output (position 1) to the taps; SW_F1..SW_F6 pick the tap (1 ohm = selected).
C C68B p2 f1 68n
C CF1 f1 f2 4n7
C CF2 f2 f3 4n7
C CF3 f3 f4 2n2
C CF4 f4 f5 1n
C CF5 f5 f6 330p
R SW_F1 f1 o 1
R SW_F2 f2 o 1e12
R SW_F3 f3 o 1e12
R SW_F4 f4 o 1e12
R SW_F5 f5 o 1e12
R SW_F6 f6 o 1e12
* The power amp's input: 100k to ground (then 100k into the first grid).
R RPI o 0 100k
